	<text xml:lang="la">
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">En mitto, doctissime <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName>, proposition[es <persName ref="p8441">Sve]nckfeldii</persName><note xml:id="fna" type="footnote" n="a"><hi>Text beim Öffnen des Siegels beschädigt.</hi></note><note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" n="1">Gemeint ist wohl das 1543 entstandene, zunächst nur handschriftlich verbreitete "Summarium von zwaierlai stande, ampt unnd erkandtnus Christi" (lat. "Collatio duorum statuum carnis Christi") von <persName ref="p8441">Kaspar Schwenckfeld</persName> (<bibl source="b169">CSch</bibl> VIII 724-753, Nr. 425). Die von <persName ref="p8440">Schuler</persName> übersandte Abschrift liegt nicht vor. <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> sandte sie an <persName ref="p8049">Vadian</persName> weiter; s. unten <ref target="file11907">Nr. 1861</ref>.</note>, quas nuper ex illius authographo clam ad <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>manus meas perveniente exscripse[ram].<pb type="edition" next="85"/></s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">[P]rodit<note xml:id="fnb" type="footnote" n="b"><hi>Text beim Öffnen des Siegels beschädigt.</hi></note> tandem venena sua lubricus anguis, quę <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>hac unica hypochrisi obtrusit vafre secure stertentibus et parum oculatis hominibus, qui <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>non simplici veritate, sed sinuosis huiusmodi cavillationibus gaudent.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Primo articulo<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2"><bibl source="b169">CSch</bibl> VIII 737, 7-12 (lat.: <bibl source="b169">CSch</bibl> VIII 734, 14-21).</note> <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>apertis atque disertis verbis negat aut veram humanitatem in Christo aut infinitam dei <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>substantiam mortalitati et corruptibilitati facit obnoxiam.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Si primum plane confundit et in dubium <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>vertit negotium redemptionis nostrae, quod in cruce moriens secundum veram humanitatem patravit, <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>negat articulum fidei, quo natum ex<note xml:id="fnc" type="footnote" n="c">ex <hi>irrtümlich wiederholt.</hi></note> Maria virgine Christum vere credimus et in univer<lb xml:id="p1z9"/>sa confitetur ecclesia,<note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3">Wie im apostolischen Glaubensbekenntnis (Denzinger 30).</note> negat item catastrophen omnium miseriarum electorum dei, futuram scilicet corporum <lb xml:id="p1z10"/>resurrectionem transfigurandaque corpora nostra humilia, ut conformia reddat corpori suo <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>glorioso.</s>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la">Vah, quot errorum plaustra secum vehit<note xml:id="fnd" type="footnote" n="d">vehit <hi>über der Zeile nachgetragen.</hi></note> frons huius scripti!</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">De recessu abstrusiore quid <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>horrendi non timeas erupturum?</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Porro, si infinitam dei substantiam mortalitati et cor<lb xml:id="p1z13"/>ruptibilitati<note xml:id="fne" type="footnote" n="e"><hi>In der Vorlage</hi> corruptibilati.</note> facit obnoxiam (nam in tertio articulo<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4"><bibl source="b169">CSch</bibl> VIII 737, 20-30 (lat.: <bibl source="b169">CSch</bibl> VIII 734, 28-33; 736, 1-4).</note> filium dei Iesum Christum secundum utranque <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>naturam cruci suffixum adfirmat, quam inpiam sententiam contraria nostra, quae adpinxit, <lb xml:id="p1z15"/>plenius confirmant), iam deum plane tollit, qui iuxta substantiam in Christo infinitus, immort<lb xml:id="p1z16"/>alis est et incorruptibilis.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Si enim Christus secundum naturam humanam naturalis dei filius est <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>et humanitas Christi in tempore initium sumpsit vereque Christus secundum eam naturam mor<lb xml:id="p1z18"/>talis et omnibus naturae calumniis excepto peccato subiectus per omnia similis factus est fratribus <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>testante apostolo,<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5">Vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Hebr 2. 17</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>4. 15.</ref></cit></note> deus praeterea „in carne non ex intervallo agens aut sicut in prophetis loquens <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>coniunctam ei humanitatem retinuit, per quam similem nostrae carnem recipiens omnem ad se <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>traxit humanitatem<note xml:id="fnf" type="footnote" n="f"><hi>Vor</hi> humanitatem <hi>gestrichenes</hi> hu <hi>und</hi> ad se.</note>“, inquit <persName ref="p18887">Basilius</persName>,<note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" n="6"><persName ref="p8440">Schuler</persName> zitiert nahezu wörtlich aus der <persName ref="p18887">Basilius d.Gr.</persName> zugeschriebenen "Homilia in sanctam Christi generationem" in der Übersetzung von <persName ref="p6941">Raphael Volaterranus</persName>; die zitierte Stelle u.a. in: Basilii Magni [...] Opera [...], <placeName ref="l378">Paris</placeName> (<persName ref="p4227">Josse Badius</persName>) 1520, f. 135r. (nach einer jüngeren Übersetzung auch in <bibl source="b445">MPG</bibl> XXXI 1460). - <persName ref="p18887">Basilius d.Gr.</persName> von <placeName ref="l1399">Caesarea</placeName>, einer der drei großen kappadokischen Kirchenlehrer, 329/330-379, war ab 370 Bischof von <placeName ref="l1399">Caesarea (Kayseri, Türkei)</placeName>. Zur gelegentlichen Zitierung seiner Schriften durch <persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> s. etwa <bibl source="b295">HBSR</bibl> II 78; <bibl source="b296">HBTS</bibl> III 1210. - Lit.: Wolf-Dieter <hi>Hauschild,</hi> in: <bibl source="b641">TRE</bibl> V 301-313.</note> Caesariensis episcopus, iam deus secundum suam naturam <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>passus est mortalis et corruptibilis, non<note xml:id="fng" type="footnote" n="g"><hi>Vor</hi> non <hi>gestrichenes</hi> et.</note> est aeternus <foreign xml:lang="el">ἄλϕα καὶ ὦ</foreign><note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7"><cit type="bible"><ref>Apk 1, 8</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>21, 6</ref></cit>; <cit type="bible"><ref>22, 13.</ref></cit></note>, in quo tunc, <lb xml:id="p1z23"/>obsecro, spes<note xml:id="fnh" type="footnote" n="h"><hi>Vor</hi> spes <hi>gestrichenes</hi> tunc.</note> nostra tute collocanda?</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la"><foreign xml:lang="de">Ach,</foreign> bone deus, quę mala adobruunt<pb type="edition" next="86"/> ecclesiam tuam anxie <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>sanguine Christi paratam!</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Hae sunt apocalypses et obtasiae<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8">Griech. <foreign xml:lang="el">ὀπτασία</foreign>, Vision.</note>, quibus sese magni venditat inerti <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>populo simplicique plebeculę vere mutabundus ille terque quaterque miser plenis buccis.</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z26"/>Hec horrenda monstra hiis tantum summopere<note xml:id="fni" type="footnote" n="i"><hi>Vor</hi> summopere <hi>ein gestrichener, unlesbarer Wortanfang.</hi></note> grata sunt, quibus cordi est<note xml:id="fnk" type="footnote" n="k">quibus cordi est <hi>am Rande nachgetragen.</hi></note> periculosa novitas quique nec <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>micam succi christianę religionis hactenus degustarunt.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Sed vero dei iuditio sic mendaciis <lb xml:id="p1z28"/>ficta fucataque<note xml:id="fnl" type="footnote" n="l">fucataque <hi>korrigiert aus</hi> fucatique.</note> veritatis spetie oblitis inescari oportet, quibus fastidio simplex est veritas.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z29"/>Dominus concedat nobis spiritus sui fervorem adeoque multam parrhisian<note xml:id="fn9" type="footnote" n="9">Griech. <foreign xml:lang="el">παρρησία</foreign>, freimütige Rede.</note> veritatem intrepide <lb xml:id="p1z30"/>adserendi.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Adversus tantas pestes ecclesiarum adferam et ego de talento michi concredito.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z31"/>Legi quam diligentissime (ut tua omnia soleo) ea, que passim in commentariis tuis super Mathei <lb xml:id="p1z32"/>et Ioannis euangelico ν[<note xml:id="fn10" type="footnote" n="10"><persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Kommentare zum Matthäus- und zum Johannesevangelium waren 1542 bzw. 1543 erschienen; s. <bibl source="b286">HBBibl</bibl> I 144. 153.</note>!] contra hunc horrendissimum errorem edidisti,<note xml:id="fn11" type="footnote" n="11">Zu der in den beiden Kommentaren eingestreuten Kritik an der Christologie <persName ref="p8441">Schwenckfelds</persName> s. bes. <bibl source="b15">HBBW XII</bibl> <ref target="file11717">[Nr. 1673]</ref> 206, Anm. 5, bzw. <bibl source="b16">HBBW XIII</bibl> 232, 19-21.</note> que michi profecto gratissima <lb xml:id="p1z33"/>sunt non tantum tuo, sed multo magis veritatis nomine, cuius solius ingenium est conscientias obfirmare <lb xml:id="p1z34"/>et tranquillas reddere.</s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la">Dominus det, ut quam diutissime ecclesię Christi et nobis prodesse valeas.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z35"/>Ego colligo super hoc negotio omnium patrum sententias, quos vel in bibliotheca mea habeo <lb xml:id="p1z36"/>vel aliunde corradere possum.</s>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la">Diligenter illorum scripta pro mea tenuitate perlustro.</s>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z37"/>Hinc quottidie clarius video inpiissimum illum hypochritam inauditos et infinitos erro<lb xml:id="p1z38"/>res alias adflictę ecclesię obtrudere; sed dominus tandem palam faciet hominis perversi <lb xml:id="p1z39"/>imposturam.</s>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la">Potes d. d. <persName ref="p8049">Vadiano</persName> hosce <persName ref="p8441">Svenckfeldii</persName> errores mittere, si illi nondum visos putaris<note xml:id="fn12" type="footnote" n="12"><persName ref="p495">Bullinger</persName> übersandte <persName ref="p8441">Schwenckfelds</persName> Schrift am 8. März an <persName ref="p8049">Vadian</persName>; s. unten <ref target="file11907">Nr. 1861</ref>.</note>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z40"/>De <persName ref="p8312">Cochleo</persName>, Sorbonico monstro, paucis diebus ad me <persName ref="p1055">Frechtus</persName> meus in hec verba scripsit:<note xml:id="fn13" type="footnote" n="13">Der Brief <persName ref="p1055">Martin Frechts</persName> an <persName ref="p8440">Schuler</persName> scheint nicht erhalten zu sein.</note> „<persName ref="p8312">Cochleus</persName> <lb xml:id="p1z41"/>etiam contra <persName ref="p495">Bullingerum</persName> nostrum aliquid ędidit<note xml:id="fn14" type="footnote" n="14">Vgl. oben <ref target="file11885">Nr. 1839</ref>, Anm. 2.</note> dignum profecto Rotzlefflio<note xml:id="fn15" type="footnote" n="15">Die Anwendung des gängigen Schimpfwortes "Rotzlöffel" (s. <bibl source="b260">Grimm</bibl> VIII 1330) auf <persName ref="p8312">Cochläus</persName> geht auf <persName ref="p1974">Luther</persName> zurück; s. <bibl source="b671">WA</bibl> XXXVIII 141, 6f.</note>“ etc.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p18538">Imperator</persName> 19. <lb xml:id="p1z42"/>ianuarii <placeName ref="l471">Spiram</placeName> comitia celebraturus venit<note xml:id="fn16" type="footnote" n="16">Das Gerücht von der Ankunft Kaiser <persName ref="p18538">Karls V.</persName> in <placeName ref="l471">Speyer</placeName> war verfrüht; s. oben <ref target="file11883">Nr. 1837</ref>, Anm. 5.</note>.</s>
					<s n="24" xml:lang="la">Mussitant nonnulli apud nos <placeName ref="l862">Helvetios</placeName> <lb xml:id="p1z43"/>evangelicos etiam Turcomastigem<note xml:id="fn17" type="footnote" n="17">Türkengeißler (iron.); s. <bibl source="b316">Hoven</bibl> 215 s.v. mastix.</note> <persName ref="p20225">Gallum</persName><note xml:id="fn18" type="footnote" n="18">König <persName ref="p20225">Franz I.</persName></note> sub<pb type="edition" next="87"/> appetens ver velle iuvare<note xml:id="fn19" type="footnote" n="19">An der <placeName ref="l21">Badener</placeName> Tagsatzung vom 17. März wandten sich <placeName ref="l587">Zürich</placeName> und <placeName ref="l41">Bern</placeName> wie bereits früher entschieden gegen ein <placeName ref="l832">französisches</placeName> Unterstützungsgesuch; s. <bibl source="b197">EA</bibl> IV/1d 356.</note>.</s>
					<s n="25" xml:lang="la"><persName ref="p19981">Papa</persName><note xml:id="fn20" type="footnote" n="20"><persName ref="p19981">Paul III.</persName></note> in hoc est totus<note xml:id="fnm" type="footnote" n="m"><hi>Vor</hi> totus <hi>gestrichenes</hi> ut.</note>, <lb xml:id="p1z44"/>ut novos cardinales creet;<note xml:id="fn21" type="footnote" n="21">Zu den Gerüchten über neue Kardinalsernennungen s. oben <ref target="file11883">Nr. 1837</ref>, 10f.</note> rubros enim galeros ante paucos annos in <placeName ref="l832">Gallia</placeName> paraverat.</s>
					<s n="26" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z45"/>Iam incipit satis diu venales vendere.</s>
					<s n="27" xml:lang="la">Sic antichristus arctius sibi sua copulat mancipia.</s>
					<s n="28" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z46"/>Dum hęc scribo, cesar apud nos <placeName ref="l320">Meminge</placeName> militem colligit.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="29" xml:lang="la">Vina consuli nostro <persName ref="p1257">Funckio</persName><note xml:id="fn22" type="footnote" n="22"><persName ref="p1257">Balthasar Funk</persName>.</note> <lb xml:id="p1z47"/>e tua paenu<note xml:id="fnn" type="footnote" n="n"><hi>Vielleicht als</hi> poenu <hi>zu lesen.</hi></note><note xml:id="fn23" type="footnote" n="23">Lat. penus, Vorrat.</note> vendita degustavi.</s>
					<s n="30" xml:lang="la">Ago simul cum uxore<note xml:id="fn24" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="24">[...], <persName ref="p19837">geb. Lübegger</persName>.</note> mea tibi gratias pro tuo in me dono, <lb xml:id="p1z48"/>mi frater charissime.</s>
					<s n="31" xml:lang="la">Valeo cum liberis<note xml:id="fn25" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="25">Zu <persName ref="p8440">Schulers</persName> Kindern s. <bibl source="b16">HBBW XIII</bibl> <ref target="file11760">[Nr. 1715]</ref> 66, Anm. 19.</note> et calefactrice uxore mea per dominum.</s>
					<s n="32" xml:lang="la">Ut tu <lb xml:id="p1z49"/>cum costa<note xml:id="fn26" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="26"><persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Ehefrau (vgl. <cit type="bible"><ref>Gen 2, 21f</ref></cit>) <persName ref="p8051">Anna, geb. Adlischwyer</persName>.</note> tua totaque familia valeas, optamus ex animo.</s>
					<s n="33" xml:lang="la" ana="salute">Salutant te fratres mei symiste<note xml:id="fn27" type="footnote" ana="lex" n="27">Symmystae, Amtsbrüder.</note>, <lb xml:id="p1z50"/>maxime <persName ref="p330">Bartholomeus Bertlinus</persName>, una cum consule <persName ref="p1257">Funckio</persName>.</s>
					<s n="34" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell">Praesente nunctio<note xml:id="fn28" type="footnote" n="28">Unbekannt.</note> rescribe, mi <persName ref="p495">Bullingere</persName>, <lb xml:id="p1z51"/>et vale <persName ref="p8440">Gervasiumque</persName> tuum, ut soles, ama.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="35" xml:lang="la">Date <placeName ref="l320">Meminge</placeName>, 31. ianuarii 1544.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="36" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z52"/><persName ref="p8440">Gervasius <span type="pronoun">tuus</span> Scolasticus</persName><lb xml:id="p1z53"/>.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="37" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Ornatissimo viro domino <persName ref="p495">Heinricho <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>Bullingero</persName>, <placeName ref="l587">Tigurinę</placeName> ecclesie antistiti <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>vigilantissimo, singulari amico et fratri <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>longe charissimo etc.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
